<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikhail Artemyevich Muravyov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1880">1880</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikhail Muravyov was a Russian army officer and Left Socialist Revolutionary who commanded Red forces after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>. In January and February 1918 he led the Bolshevik advance on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, shelling the city and carrying out mass executions after its capture. Appointed commander of the Eastern Front, he rebelled against the Bolsheviks at Simbirsk in July 1918 and was killed while being arrested.</p></div>
